<%!-- The single flash group for every Core LiveView and controller render.

Placement is load-bearing, not incidental. This layout is part of the
LiveView's own rendered tree, so a `put_flash/3` raised while the page is
live patches this group. A root layout is rendered once, on the initial HTTP
response, and is never diffed afterwards, so a group placed there shows only
the flash that was already in the session at mount and silently swallows
every later one.

No root layout and no page template may render a second group: both would
render, and the user would read the same sentence twice. --%>
<.flash_group flash={@flash} id="app-flash-group" />
{@inner_content}
